  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Congregation Notice",
    "overview": "A light, restrained Swedish congregation notice: warm paper, deep green ink, muted brass and fine rules. The service feels calm and legible in a Friday-prayer setting, with Swedish interface text and a distinct Arabic typographic voice.\n\nThe system is code-led and flat. Clear typography and deliberate space carry the identity across public listening, sign-in and broadcast administration. The approved direction uses self-hosted fonts and no decorative raster assets. PRODUCT.md supplies the durable language and identity constraints; individual screen composition belongs to the surface contract.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper with deep green text and actions.",
      "Serif headings, Arabic calligraphy and practical sans-serif controls.",
      "Fine rules and compact, subtly squared controls.",
      "Readable listening states and explicit broadcast feedback."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Ink and Paper Rule",
        "body": "Use green for text and primary actions, brass for restrained emphasis, and semantic green or red for operational state. Status always includes words alongside color.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Reading Priority Rule",
        "body": "Reduce introductory type in the connected state so controls and Swedish captions become the main reading surface.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Notice Rule",
        "body": "Separate content with space, thin rules and state fills; retain the flat document character.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the existing paper, green and brass roles across public and admin screens.",
      "Do preserve the separate Arabic and Swedish type voices and correct script direction.",
